// Fitting the kind and the difficulty of each main-set item to the learner. The
// planner picks an item per concept by how well its difficulty fits (fit_of.id);
// this step, run on the finished plan of a version 2 pack, may swap an item for
// another practice item of the same concept that suits the learner's behaviour
// better: its kind ranks higher for the learner's level on the concept
// (kinds.id), and its difficulty lies within plan_kind_slack of the item it
// replaces, raised by plan_difficulty_step when the learner's latest attempt on
// the concept was fluent (clean, confident, quick). The score of a candidate is
// its kind rank times plan_kind_weight plus its distance from the target
// difficulty; the lowest wins and the item already planned wins a tie, so a swap
// happens only for a reason, and the reason is added to the row (row.id).
// plan_candidate_score scores one item, plan_link_score one link of the book
// (answering plan_item_none when the link is not an eligible alternative: another
// concept, a held-out item, or an item already in the session), and
// plan_first_concept finds the concept an item practises first.

plan_first_concept(Plan_book plan_book, int plan_item_number) {
  int plan_at = 0;
  int plan_first = 0 - 1;
  while (plan_at < len(plan_book.links.link_items) && plan_first < 0) {
    if (plan_book.links.link_items[plan_at] == plan_item_number) {
      plan_first = plan_book.links.link_concepts[plan_at];
    }
    plan_at = plan_at + 1;
  }
} return int plan_first;
